-- Employment Insurance Regulations (SOR/96-332), regulations 56, 56.1 and 57: WRITE-OFF OF AMOUNTS WRONGLY PAID,
-- PENALTIES AND INTEREST; INTEREST ON AMOUNTS OWING TO HER MAJESTY; and DEDUCTIONS FROM BENEFITS FOR PAYMENTS TO
-- GOVERNMENTS AND AUTHORITIES.
-- Written by the piece agent er3 (Sonnet 5.5) on 2026-10-24 from the unofficial plain-text rendering
-- SOR-96-332.txt; nothing here is claimed to be verified against the official text.
--
-- The Commission's power to write off (reg 56) and to waive interest (reg 56.1(8)) is a power: the rules say whether
-- its conditions are met, never whether it is used. What the Commission "considers" (reg 56(1)(f)) is an input.
-- Out of range: ss 38, 39, 41.1, 43, 45, 46, 46.1, 47, 65, 65.1, 65.2 (penalties, warnings and amounts owing, pieces
-- ei1 and ei3), ss 41, 52, 111 (reconsideration, ei1 and ei4), ss 135, 136 (offences, ei4), s 42(3) (deductions, ei1),
-- Part IV (the retrospective rulings, ei3), the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act, the Criminal Code and the Indian Act
-- (outside the texts). The day reg 56.1 came into force is not in the text: an input.

§ `Regulation 56 -- write-off of amounts wrongly paid, penalties and interest`

-- (1)(a) The total of the penalties and amounts owing by the debtor to Her Majesty under any program administered by
-- the Department of Employment and Social Development, with the interest accrued on them, does not exceed $100 (so
-- $100 is within); no benefit period is currently running in respect of the debtor; and the debtor is not
-- currently making regular payments on a repayment plan.
-- src:945 | (a) the total of the penalties and amounts, including the interest accrued on those penalties and amounts, owing by the debtor to Her Majesty under any program administered by the Department of Employment and Social Development does not exceed $100, a benefit period is not currently running in respect of the debtor and the debtor is not currently making regular payments on a repayment plan;
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 56(1)(a) (src:945)
GIVEN `the total of the penalties and amounts, including the interest accrued on them, owing by the debtor to Her Majesty under any program administered by the Department of Employment and Social Development` IS A NUMBER
      `a benefit period is currently running in respect of the debtor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the debtor is currently making regular payments on a repayment plan` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 56(1)(a) the amounts owing do not exceed $100 and the debtor has no benefit period running and no repayment plan` IF
        `the total of the penalties and amounts, including the interest accrued on them, owing by the debtor to Her Majesty under any program administered by the Department of Employment and Social Development` AT MOST 100
    AND NOT (`a benefit period is currently running in respect of the debtor`)
    AND NOT (`the debtor is currently making regular payments on a repayment plan`)

-- (1)(d) An undischarged bankrupt in respect of whom the final dividend has been paid and the trustee has been
-- discharged.
-- src:948 | (d) the debtor is an undischarged bankrupt in respect of whom the final dividend has been paid and the trustee has been discharged;
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 56(1)(d) (src:948)
GIVEN `the debtor is an undischarged bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the final dividend has been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trustee has been discharged` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 56(1)(d) the debtor is an undischarged bankrupt whose final dividend has been paid and whose trustee has been discharged` IF
        `the debtor is an undischarged bankrupt`
    AND `the final dividend has been paid`
    AND `the trustee has been discharged`

-- (1)(e) The overpayment does not arise from an error made by the debtor or from a false or misleading declaration
-- or representation made by the debtor (whether or not the debtor knew it to be false or misleading), but arises
-- from (i) a retrospective decision or ruling under Part IV of the Act, or (ii) a retrospective decision under Part I
-- or IV in relation to benefits paid under s 25.
-- src:949 | (e) the overpayment does not arise from an error made by the debtor or as a result of a false or misleading declaration or representation made by the debtor, whether the debtor knew it to be false or misleading or not, but arises from
-- src:950 | (i) a retrospective decision or ruling made under Part IV of the Act, or
-- src:951 | (ii) a retrospective decision made under Part I or IV of the Act in relation to benefits paid under section 25 of the Act; or
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 56(1)(e) (src:949-951)
GIVEN `the overpayment arises from an error made by the debtor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the overpayment arises from a false or misleading declaration or representation made by the debtor, whether the debtor knew it to be false or misleading or not` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it arises from a retrospective decision or ruling made under Part IV of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it arises from a retrospective decision made under Part I or IV of the Act in relation to benefits paid under section 25 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 56(1)(e) the overpayment arises from a retrospective decision and not from the debtor's error or false declaration` IF
        NOT (`the overpayment arises from an error made by the debtor`)
    AND NOT (`the overpayment arises from a false or misleading declaration or representation made by the debtor, whether the debtor knew it to be false or misleading or not`)
    AND (   `it arises from a retrospective decision or ruling made under Part IV of the Act`
         OR `it arises from a retrospective decision made under Part I or IV of the Act in relation to benefits paid under section 25 of the Act`)

-- (1)(f) The Commission considers, having regard to all the circumstances, that (i) the penalty, amount or interest is
-- uncollectable, (ii) repayment would result in undue hardship to the debtor, or (iii) the administrative costs of
-- collecting it would likely equal or exceed it. What the Commission considers is a judgment of its own: each limb is
-- an input named for that judgment.
-- src:952 | (f) the Commission considers that, having regard to all the circumstances,
-- src:953 | (i) the penalty or amount, or the interest accrued on it, is uncollectable,
-- src:954 | (ii) the repayment of the penalty or amount, or the interest accrued on it, would result in undue hardship to the debtor, or
-- src:955 | (iii) the administrative costs of collecting the penalty or amount, or the interest accrued on it, would likely equal or exceed the penalty, amount or interest to be collected.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 56(1)(f) (src:952-955)
GIVEN `the Commission considers that the penalty or amount, or the interest accrued on it, is uncollectable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission considers that its repayment would result in undue hardship to the debtor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission considers that the administrative costs of collecting it would likely equal or exceed what is to be collected` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 56(1)(f) the Commission considers it uncollectable, a hardship or not worth collecting` IF
       `the Commission considers that the penalty or amount, or the interest accrued on it, is uncollectable`
    OR `the Commission considers that its repayment would result in undue hardship to the debtor`
    OR `the Commission considers that the administrative costs of collecting it would likely equal or exceed what is to be collected`

-- (1) A penalty owing under s 38, 39 or 65.1 of the Act, or an amount payable under s 43, 45, 46, 46.1 or 65, or the
-- interest accrued on the penalty or amount, may be written off by the Commission if any one of (a) to (f) holds
-- ((b) the debtor is deceased; (c) the debtor is a discharged bankrupt). The Commission's power is a power; the
-- debtor is liable to its exercise and has no claim to it.
-- src:944 | 56 (1) A penalty owing under section 38, 39 or 65.1 of the Act or an amount payable under section 43, 45, 46, 46.1 or 65 of the Act, or the interest accrued on the penalty or amount, may be written off by the Commission if
-- src:945 | (a) the total of the penalties and amounts, including the interest accrued on those penalties and amounts, owing by the debtor to Her Majesty under any program administered by the Department of Employment and Social Development does not exceed $100, a benefit period is not currently running in respect of the debtor and the debtor is not currently making regular payments on a repayment plan;
-- src:946 | (b) the debtor is deceased;
-- src:947 | (c) the debtor is a discharged bankrupt;
-- src:948 | (d) the debtor is an undischarged bankrupt in respect of whom the final dividend has been paid and the trustee has been discharged;
-- src:949 | (e) the overpayment does not arise from an error made by the debtor or as a result of a false or misleading declaration or representation made by the debtor, whether the debtor knew it to be false or misleading or not, but arises from
-- src:950 | (i) a retrospective decision or ruling made under Part IV of the Act, or
-- src:951 | (ii) a retrospective decision made under Part I or IV of the Act in relation to benefits paid under section 25 of the Act; or
-- src:952 | (f) the Commission considers that, having regard to all the circumstances,
-- src:953 | (i) the penalty or amount, or the interest accrued on it, is uncollectable,
-- src:954 | (ii) the repayment of the penalty or amount, or the interest accrued on it, would result in undue hardship to the debtor, or
-- src:955 | (iii) the administrative costs of collecting the penalty or amount, or the interest accrued on it, would likely equal or exceed the penalty, amount or interest to be collected.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 56(1) (src:944-955)
GIVEN `it is a penalty owing under section 38, 39 or 65.1 of the Act, an amount payable under section 43, 45, 46, 46.1 or 65 of the Act, or the interest accrued on one of them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (a) holds` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the debtor is deceased` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the debtor is a discharged bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (d) holds` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (e) holds` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (f) holds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 56(1) the conditions on which the Commission may write off a penalty, an amount payable or the interest are met` IF
        `it is a penalty owing under section 38, 39 or 65.1 of the Act, an amount payable under section 43, 45, 46, 46.1 or 65 of the Act, or the interest accrued on one of them`
    AND (   `paragraph (a) holds`
         OR `the debtor is deceased`
         OR `the debtor is a discharged bankrupt`
         OR `paragraph (d) holds`
         OR `paragraph (e) holds`
         OR `paragraph (f) holds`)

-- (2) The portion of an amount owing under s 47 or 65 in respect of benefits received more than 12 months before the
-- Commission notifies the debtor of the overpayment, with the interest accrued on it, may be written off if (a) the
-- overpayment does not arise from an error made by the debtor or from a false or misleading declaration or
-- representation made by the debtor; and (b) it arises as a result of (i) a delay or error made by the Commission in
-- processing a claim, (ii) retrospective control procedures or review initiated by the Commission, (iii) an error
-- made on the record of employment by the employer, (iv) an incorrect calculation by the employer of the debtor's
-- insurable earnings or hours, or (v) an error in insuring the employment or other activity of the debtor.
-- src:956 | (2) The portion of an amount owing under section 47 or 65 of the Act in respect of benefits received more than 12 months before the Commission notifies the debtor of the overpayment, including the interest accrued on it, may be written off by the Commission if
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 56(2) (src:956)
DECLARE `er3 Overpaid benefit` HAS
    `the day on which the benefit was received` IS A DATE
    `the overpayment in respect of it` IS A NUMBER

-- src:956 | (2) The portion of an amount owing under section 47 or 65 of the Act in respect of benefits received more than 12 months before the Commission notifies the debtor of the overpayment, including the interest accrued on it, may be written off by the Commission if
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 56(2) (src:956)
GIVEN `the day on which the benefit was received` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the Commission notifies the debtor of the overpayment` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 56(2) the benefit was received more than 12 months before the Commission notified the debtor` IF
    (`add months` `the day on which the benefit was received` 12) LESS THAN `the day on which the Commission notifies the debtor of the overpayment`

-- src:957 | (a) the overpayment does not arise from an error made by the debtor or as a result of a false or misleading declaration or representation made by the debtor, whether the debtor knew it to be false or misleading or not; and
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 56(2)(a) (src:957)
GIVEN `the overpayment arises from an error made by the debtor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the overpayment arises from a false or misleading declaration or representation made by the debtor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 56(2)(a) the overpayment does not arise from the debtor's error or false declaration` IF
        NOT (`the overpayment arises from an error made by the debtor`)
    AND NOT (`the overpayment arises from a false or misleading declaration or representation made by the debtor`)

-- src:958 | (b) the overpayment arises as a result of
-- src:959 | (i) a delay or error made by the Commission in processing a claim for benefits,
-- src:960 | (ii) retrospective control procedures or a retrospective review initiated by the Commission,
-- src:961 | (iii) an error made on the record of employment by the employer,
-- src:962 | (iv) an incorrect calculation by the employer of the debtor's insurable earnings or hours of insurable employment, or
-- src:963 | (v) an error in insuring the employment or other activity of the debtor.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 56(2)(b) (src:958-963)
GIVEN `a delay or error made by the Commission in processing a claim for benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `retrospective control procedures or a retrospective review initiated by the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an error made on the record of employment by the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an incorrect calculation by the employer of the debtor's insurable earnings or hours of insurable employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an error in insuring the employment or other activity of the debtor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 56(2)(b) the overpayment arises as a result of one of the five causes` IF
       `a delay or error made by the Commission in processing a claim for benefits`
    OR `retrospective control procedures or a retrospective review initiated by the Commission`
    OR `an error made on the record of employment by the employer`
    OR `an incorrect calculation by the employer of the debtor's insurable earnings or hours of insurable employment`
    OR `an error in insuring the employment or other activity of the debtor`

-- The portion that may be written off: the overpayments in respect of benefits received more than 12 months
-- before the notification, with the interest accrued on them, if (a) and (b) hold; otherwise nothing under (2).
-- src:956 | (2) The portion of an amount owing under section 47 or 65 of the Act in respect of benefits received more than 12 months before the Commission notifies the debtor of the overpayment, including the interest accrued on it, may be written off by the Commission if
-- src:957 | (a) the overpayment does not arise from an error made by the debtor or as a result of a false or misleading declaration or representation made by the debtor, whether the debtor knew it to be false or misleading or not; and
-- src:958 | (b) the overpayment arises as a result of
-- src:959 | (i) a delay or error made by the Commission in processing a claim for benefits,
-- src:960 | (ii) retrospective control procedures or a retrospective review initiated by the Commission,
-- src:961 | (iii) an error made on the record of employment by the employer,
-- src:962 | (iv) an incorrect calculation by the employer of the debtor's insurable earnings or hours of insurable employment, or
-- src:963 | (v) an error in insuring the employment or other activity of the debtor.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 56(2) (src:956-963)
GIVEN overpaid IS A LIST OF `er3 Overpaid benefit`
      `the day on which the Commission notifies the debtor of the overpayment` IS A DATE
      `the interest accrued on that portion` IS A NUMBER
      `paragraph (a) holds` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (b) holds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 56(2) the portion of the amount owing that may be written off` IS
    IF `paragraph (a) holds` AND `paragraph (b) holds`
    THEN (sum (map (GIVEN x YIELD x's `the overpayment in respect of it`)
                   (filter (GIVEN x YIELD `reg 56(2) the benefit was received more than 12 months before the Commission notified the debtor` (x's `the day on which the benefit was received`) `the day on which the Commission notifies the debtor of the overpayment`) overpaid)))
         PLUS `the interest accrued on that portion`
    ELSE 0

§ `Regulation 56.1 -- interest on amounts owing to Her Majesty`

-- (1) "average bank rate" is the simple arithmetic mean of the bank rates established during the month before the
-- month for which interest is being calculated. The bank rate is the Bank of Canada's weekly minimum rate for its
-- short-term advances to members of the Canadian Payments Association: the rates are inputs, as fractions (4.25% is
-- 0.0425). No rate, no mean: NOTHING.
-- src:967 | average bank rate means the simple arithmetic mean of the bank rates that are established during the month before the month in respect of which interest is being calculated. (taux d'escompte moyen)
-- src:968 | bank rate means the rate of interest established weekly by the Bank of Canada as the minimum rate at which the Bank of Canada makes short-term advances to members of the Canadian Payments Association. (taux d'escompte)
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 56.1(1) "average bank rate", "bank rate" (src:967-968)
GIVEN `the bank rates established during the month before the month in respect of which interest is being calculated` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 56.1(1) the average bank rate` IS
    IF null `the bank rates established during the month before the month in respect of which interest is being calculated`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST ((sum `the bank rates established during the month before the month in respect of which interest is being calculated`) DIVIDED BY (count `the bank rates established during the month before the month in respect of which interest is being calculated`))

-- (2) If an appeal in respect of a penalty or warning results in its rescission, or the claimant is eventually
-- acquitted in a prosecution, the debt that was the subject of the decision is not a debt arising from an act or omission.
-- src:970 | (2) If an appeal in respect of a penalty imposed under section 38, 39 or 65.1 of the Act or of a warning issued under section 41.1 of the Act results in the rescinding of the penalty or warning or if a claimant is eventually acquitted in a prosecution under section 135 or 136 of the Act or under the Criminal Code, the debt that was the subject of the decision is not a debt arising from an act or omission.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 56.1(2) (src:970)
GIVEN `an appeal in respect of the penalty or warning results in its rescinding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is eventually acquitted in a prosecution under section 135 or 136 of the Act or under the Criminal Code` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 56.1(2) the debt is not a debt arising from an act or omission` IF
       `an appeal in respect of the penalty or warning results in its rescinding`
    OR `the claimant is eventually acquitted in a prosecution under section 135 or 136 of the Act or under the Criminal Code`

-- (1) "debt arising from an act or omission" means an amount payable under s 43, 45, 46, 46.1 or 65 in respect of which a
-- penalty was imposed under s 38, 39 or 65.1, or a warning was issued under s 41.1, or a prosecution was undertaken
-- under s 135 or 136 or under the Criminal Code; and includes an amount payable under s 38, 39 or 65.1 and an amount
-- payable as a result of the judgment of a court. Subsection (2) takes a debt out of the definition.
-- src:969 | debt arising from an act or omission means an amount payable under section 43, 45, 46, 46.1 or 65 of the Act in respect of which a penalty was imposed under section 38, 39 or 65.1 of the Act or a warning was issued under section 41.1 of the Act or in respect of which a prosecution was undertaken under section 135 or 136 of the Act or under the Criminal Code, and includes an amount payable under section 38, 39 or 65.1 of the Act and an amount payable as a result of the judgment of a court. (dette résultant d'un acte délictueux)
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 56.1(1) "debt arising from an act or omission" (src:969)
GIVEN `it is an amount payable under section 43, 45, 46, 46.1 or 65 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a penalty was imposed under section 38, 39 or 65.1 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a warning was issued under section 41.1 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a prosecution was undertaken under section 135 or 136 of the Act or under the Criminal Code` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an amount payable under section 38, 39 or 65.1 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an amount payable as a result of the judgment of a court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 56.1(1) debt arising from an act or omission, before subsection (2)` IF
        (   `it is an amount payable under section 43, 45, 46, 46.1 or 65 of the Act`
        AND (   `a penalty was imposed under section 38, 39 or 65.1 of the Act`
             OR `a warning was issued under section 41.1 of the Act`
             OR `a prosecution was undertaken under section 135 or 136 of the Act or under the Criminal Code`))
    OR `it is an amount payable under section 38, 39 or 65.1 of the Act`
    OR `it is an amount payable as a result of the judgment of a court`

-- (3) Interest accrues, at a rate calculated daily and compounded monthly at the average bank rate plus three per cent,
-- on all debts arising from an act or omission and owing to Her Majesty under s 47 or 65.2 on or after the day this
-- section comes into force. The day is not in the text: an input.
-- src:971 | (3) Interest accrues, at a rate that is calculated daily and compounded monthly at the average bank rate plus three per cent, on all debts arising from an act or omission and owing to Her Majesty under section 47 or 65.2 of the Act on or after the day this section comes into force.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 56.1(3) (src:971)
GIVEN `the debt is a debt arising from an act or omission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the debt is owing to Her Majesty under section 47 or 65.2 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the debt is owing` IS A DATE
      `the day on which regulation 56.1 came into force` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 56.1(3) the debt carries interest` IF
        `the debt is a debt arising from an act or omission`
    AND `the debt is owing to Her Majesty under section 47 or 65.2 of the Act`
    AND `the day on which the debt is owing` AT LEAST `the day on which regulation 56.1 came into force`

-- (3) The rate is the average bank rate plus three per cent a year.
-- src:971 | (3) Interest accrues, at a rate that is calculated daily and compounded monthly at the average bank rate plus three per cent, on all debts arising from an act or omission and owing to Her Majesty under section 47 or 65.2 of the Act on or after the day this section comes into force.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 56.1(3) (src:971)
GIVEN `the average bank rate` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 56.1(3) the annual rate of interest` IS
    CONSIDER `the average bank rate`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST rate THEN JUST (rate PLUS 3%)

-- (3) "calculated daily and compounded monthly": the interest of a month is the balance at the start of the month
-- times the annual rate times the days of the month over the days of the year; at the end of the month it is added
-- to the balance. The text does not give the number of days of the year: it is an input (fork F18). The interest is
-- not rounded: the text gives no rounding.
-- src:971 | (3) Interest accrues, at a rate that is calculated daily and compounded monthly at the average bank rate plus three per cent, on all debts arising from an act or omission and owing to Her Majesty under section 47 or 65.2 of the Act on or after the day this section comes into force.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 56.1(3) (src:971)
GIVEN `the balance at the start of the month` IS A NUMBER
      `the annual rate of interest` IS A NUMBER
      `the days of the month` IS A NUMBER
      `the days of the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 56.1(3) the interest accruing in a month` IS
    IF `the days of the year` AT MOST 0
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST ((`the balance at the start of the month` TIMES `the annual rate of interest` TIMES `the days of the month`) DIVIDED BY `the days of the year`)

-- src:971 | (3) Interest accrues, at a rate that is calculated daily and compounded monthly at the average bank rate plus three per cent, on all debts arising from an act or omission and owing to Her Majesty under section 47 or 65.2 of the Act on or after the day this section comes into force.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 56.1(3) (src:971)
GIVEN `the balance at the start of the month` IS A NUMBER
      `the interest accruing in the month` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 56.1(3) the balance at the end of the month, after compounding` IS
    CONSIDER `the interest accruing in the month`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST interest THEN JUST (`the balance at the start of the month` PLUS interest)

-- (4) The accrual of interest begins on the day on which the debtor is notified of the amount owing.
-- src:972 | (4) The accrual of interest on an amount owing to Her Majesty under section 47 or 65.2 of the Act, at the rate set out in subsection (3), begins on the day on which the debtor is notified of the amount owing.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 56.1(4) (src:972)
GIVEN `the day on which the debtor is notified of the amount owing` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `reg 56.1(4) the day on which interest begins to accrue` IS `the day on which the debtor is notified of the amount owing`

-- (5) and (6) Interest does not accrue during the period in which an appeal or other review of the decision that
-- gave rise to the obligation to pay is pending; that does not include the reconsideration of a decision by the
-- Commission under s 41, 52 or 111 of the Act.
-- src:973 | (5) Subject to subsection (6), interest does not accrue on an amount owing to Her Majesty under section 47 or 65.2 of the Act during the period in which an appeal or other review of the decision that gave rise to the obligation to pay that amount is pending.
-- src:974 | (6) An appeal or other review referred to in subsection (5) does not include the reconsideration of a decision by the Commission under section 41, 52 or 111 of the Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 56.1(5), (6) (src:973-974)
GIVEN `an appeal or other review of the decision that gave rise to the obligation to pay is pending` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the only thing pending is a reconsideration of a decision by the Commission under section 41, 52 or 111 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 56.1(5) and (6) interest does not accrue because an appeal or review is pending` IF
        `an appeal or other review of the decision that gave rise to the obligation to pay is pending`
    AND NOT (`the only thing pending is a reconsideration of a decision by the Commission under section 41, 52 or 111 of the Act`)

-- (7) The accrual ceases on the day on which (a) repayment of the amount and the interest accrued is received, (b) the
-- debtor dies, (c) the amount owed is written off under s 56, or (d) the accrued interest is written off under s 56:
-- the earliest of those that has happened. The day itself is the first without interest (fork F19).
-- src:975 | (7) The accrual of interest on an amount owing to Her Majesty under section 47 or 65.2 of the Act ceases on the day on which
-- src:976 | (a) repayment of the amount owed to Her Majesty and any interest accrued on that amount is received by Her Majesty or a duly authorized agent of Her Majesty;
-- src:977 | (b) the debtor dies;
-- src:978 | (c) the amount owed is written off under section 56; or
-- src:979 | (d) the accrued interest is written off under section 56.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 56.1(7) (src:975-979)
GIVEN `the day on which repayment of the amount owed and the interest accrued on it is received by Her Majesty or a duly authorized agent` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day on which the debtor dies` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day on which the amount owed is written off under section 56` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day on which the accrued interest is written off under section 56` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `reg 56.1(7) the day on which the accrual of interest ceases` IS
    LET days MEANS concat (map `reg 56.1 a date as a list` (LIST `the day on which repayment of the amount owed and the interest accrued on it is received by Her Majesty or a duly authorized agent`, `the day on which the debtor dies`, `the day on which the amount owed is written off under section 56`, `the day on which the accrued interest is written off under section 56`))
    IN IF null days THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST (Date (minimum (map (GIVEN d YIELD Day d) days)))

-- Interest accrues on a given day: it is after the day it begins, the debt carries interest under (3), no appeal or
-- review is pending under (5), and the accrual has not ceased under (7).
-- src:971 | (3) Interest accrues, at a rate that is calculated daily and compounded monthly at the average bank rate plus three per cent, on all debts arising from an act or omission and owing to Her Majesty under section 47 or 65.2 of the Act on or after the day this section comes into force.
-- src:972 | (4) The accrual of interest on an amount owing to Her Majesty under section 47 or 65.2 of the Act, at the rate set out in subsection (3), begins on the day on which the debtor is notified of the amount owing.
-- src:973 | (5) Subject to subsection (6), interest does not accrue on an amount owing to Her Majesty under section 47 or 65.2 of the Act during the period in which an appeal or other review of the decision that gave rise to the obligation to pay that amount is pending.
-- src:974 | (6) An appeal or other review referred to in subsection (5) does not include the reconsideration of a decision by the Commission under section 41, 52 or 111 of the Act.
-- src:975 | (7) The accrual of interest on an amount owing to Her Majesty under section 47 or 65.2 of the Act ceases on the day on which
-- src:976 | (a) repayment of the amount owed to Her Majesty and any interest accrued on that amount is received by Her Majesty or a duly authorized agent of Her Majesty;
-- src:977 | (b) the debtor dies;
-- src:978 | (c) the amount owed is written off under section 56; or
-- src:979 | (d) the accrued interest is written off under section 56.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 56.1(3) to (7) (src:971-979)
GIVEN `the debt carries interest under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day for which the question is asked` IS A DATE
      `the day on which interest begins to accrue` IS A DATE
      `the accrual is suspended under subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the accrual ceases` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 56.1 interest accrues on the day` IF
        `the debt carries interest under subsection (3)`
    AND `the day for which the question is asked` AT LEAST `the day on which interest begins to accrue`
    AND NOT (`the accrual is suspended under subsection (5)`)
    AND `reg 56.1(7) the accrual has not ceased by the day` `the day on which the accrual ceases` `the day for which the question is asked`

GIVEN `the day on which the accrual ceases` IS A MAYBE DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 56.1(7) the accrual has not ceased by the day` IS
    CONSIDER `the day on which the accrual ceases`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST stop THEN day LESS THAN stop

GIVEN m IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`reg 56.1 a date as a list` m MEANS
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN NOTHING THEN EMPTY
    WHEN JUST x THEN LIST x

-- (8) The Commission may waive or reduce the interest if (a) the administrative costs of collecting the interest owing
-- would exceed the amount of that interest; (b) the interest is payable in respect of an amount in dispute where the
-- dispute has been settled, in whole or in part, in favour of the debtor; or (c) the accrual of interest on a
-- particular penalty or amount would result in undue hardship to the debtor.
-- src:980 | (8) The Commission may waive or reduce the amount of interest provided for in this section if
-- src:981 | (a) the administrative costs of collecting the interest owing would exceed the amount of that interest;
-- src:982 | (b) the interest is payable in respect of an amount in dispute where the dispute has been settled, in whole or in part, in favour of the debtor; or
-- src:983 | (c) the accrual of interest on a particular penalty or amount owing would result in undue hardship to the debtor.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 56.1(8) (src:980-983)
GIVEN `the administrative costs of collecting the interest owing` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of the interest owing` IS A NUMBER
      `the interest is payable in respect of an amount in dispute and the dispute has been settled, in whole or in part, in favour of the debtor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accrual of interest on the penalty or amount would result in undue hardship to the debtor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 56.1(8) the conditions on which the Commission may waive or reduce the interest are met` IF
       `the administrative costs of collecting the interest owing` GREATER THAN `the amount of the interest owing`
    OR `the interest is payable in respect of an amount in dispute and the dispute has been settled, in whole or in part, in favour of the debtor`
    OR `the accrual of interest on the penalty or amount would result in undue hardship to the debtor`

§ `Regulation 57 -- deductions from benefits for payments to governments and authorities`

-- The payers of (2): the Government of Canada or any of its agencies, a provincial government, a municipal
-- government, or "any other authority prescribed by this section", which by (4) is the council of an Indian band.
-- src:987 | (2) No deduction shall be made in respect of any advance or assistance or welfare payment paid by the Government of Canada or any of its agencies, a provincial or municipal government or any other authority prescribed by this section, unless
-- src:988 | (a) an arrangement has been entered into between the Commission and the Government of Canada or any of its agencies, the provincial government or the municipal government or the prescribed authority in respect of the deduction; and
-- src:989 | (b) the person to whom the payment is made has consented pursuant to subsection 42(3) of the Act to the deduction by signing the form supplied by the Commission.
-- src:990 | (3) The Commission may at any time terminate an arrangement entered into pursuant to subsection (2).
-- src:991 | (4) The council of an Indian band, referred to as a council of the band in subsection 2(1) of the Indian Act, is a prescribed authority for the purposes of subsection 42(3) of the Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 57(2), (4) (src:987-991)
DECLARE `er3 Payer of an advance, assistance or welfare payment` IS ONE OF
    `er3 payer: the Government of Canada or any of its agencies`
    `er3 payer: a provincial government`
    `er3 payer: a municipal government`
    `er3 payer: the council of an Indian band`
    `er3 payer: someone else`

-- (4) The council of an Indian band, referred to as a council of the band in subsection 2(1) of the Indian Act, is a
-- prescribed authority for the purposes of subsection 42(3) of the Act.
-- src:991 | (4) The council of an Indian band, referred to as a council of the band in subsection 2(1) of the Indian Act, is a prescribed authority for the purposes of subsection 42(3) of the Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 57(4) (src:991)
GIVEN payer IS A `er3 Payer of an advance, assistance or welfare payment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 57(4) the payer is a prescribed authority` IF
    payer EQUALS `er3 payer: the council of an Indian band`

-- (2) The payer is one of those listed: the Government of Canada or any of its agencies, a provincial or municipal
-- government, or a prescribed authority.
-- src:987 | (2) No deduction shall be made in respect of any advance or assistance or welfare payment paid by the Government of Canada or any of its agencies, a provincial or municipal government or any other authority prescribed by this section, unless
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 57(2) (src:987)
GIVEN payer IS A `er3 Payer of an advance, assistance or welfare payment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 57(2) the payer is one of those listed` IF
        payer EQUALS `er3 payer: the Government of Canada or any of its agencies`
    OR payer EQUALS `er3 payer: a provincial government`
    OR payer EQUALS `er3 payer: a municipal government`
    OR `reg 57(4) the payer is a prescribed authority` payer

-- (3) The Commission may at any time terminate an arrangement entered into under (2).
-- src:990 | (3) The Commission may at any time terminate an arrangement entered into pursuant to subsection (2).
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 57(3) (src:990)
GIVEN `an arrangement has been entered into between the Commission and the payer in respect of the deduction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission has terminated the arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 57(3) the arrangement is in force` IF
        `an arrangement has been entered into between the Commission and the payer in respect of the deduction`
    AND NOT (`the Commission has terminated the arrangement`)

-- (1) "deduction" means a deduction from benefits made by the Commission under subsection 42(3) of the Act.
-- (2) No deduction is made in respect of an advance, assistance or welfare payment paid by one of those payers unless
-- (a) an arrangement has been entered into between the Commission and the payer in respect of the deduction; and (b)
-- the person to whom the payment is made has consented under s 42(3) of the Act to the deduction by signing the
-- form supplied by the Commission. A payment of another kind is not touched by (2): NOTHING.
-- src:986 | 57 (1) In this section, deduction means a deduction from benefits that is made by the Commission pursuant to subsection 42(3) of the Act.
-- src:987 | (2) No deduction shall be made in respect of any advance or assistance or welfare payment paid by the Government of Canada or any of its agencies, a provincial or municipal government or any other authority prescribed by this section, unless
-- src:988 | (a) an arrangement has been entered into between the Commission and the Government of Canada or any of its agencies, the provincial government or the municipal government or the prescribed authority in respect of the deduction; and
-- src:989 | (b) the person to whom the payment is made has consented pursuant to subsection 42(3) of the Act to the deduction by signing the form supplied by the Commission.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 57(1), (2) (src:986-989)
GIVEN `the payment is an advance or assistance or welfare payment` IS A BOOLEAN
      payer IS A `er3 Payer of an advance, assistance or welfare payment`
      `the arrangement is in force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person to whom the payment is made has consented under subsection 42(3) of the Act to the deduction by signing the form supplied by the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 57(2) a deduction may be made from the benefits in respect of the payment` IS
    IF `the payment is an advance or assistance or welfare payment` AND `reg 57(2) the payer is one of those listed` payer
    THEN JUST (`the arrangement is in force` AND `the person to whom the payment is made has consented under subsection 42(3) of the Act to the deduction by signing the form supplied by the Commission`)
    ELSE NOTHING
